andidate**\n- **Candidate 4:** 3-day cycle with about 1.2× buffer. Shortfalls are minimal and fees are moderate. I rank it best.\n- **Candidate 5:** 3-day cycle with about 1.1× buffer. Close behind candidate 4.\n- **Candidate 0:** 4-day cycle with the lowest fees and about 1.1× buffer. Its weak spot is the batch arriving on day 10: it covers days 10–13, which need 139 units including the 70-unit peak, but only 118 are ordered. That shortfall of about 20 or more units costs roughly 300–400. Product 1 is ordered right at the forecast.\n- **Candidate 7:** 2-day cycle with about 1.2× buffer. Few shortfalls, but about 220 more in fees than the 3-day plans.\n- **Candidate 2:** 2-day cycle with about 1.12× buffer. Close to candidates 0 and 7.\n- **Candidate 3:** 3-day cycle at the forecast. Expected shortfall is about 6 units per cycle, roughly 900 lost over the month.\n- **Candidate 1:** 2-day cycle at the forecast. It has both the shortfall problem and the higher fees.\n- **Candidate 6:** daily orders. The fees alone sink it.\n\nThe less certain calls are candidates 0, 7 and 2 for the last two top-four spots. Candidates 4 and 5 look safe, and candidates 3, 1 and 6 look clearly worse."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4928, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4928}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:02:22.926Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWBGQsUfaDfKEPGNHPuc"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_